    "title": "What channel is Tennessee basketball vs Virginia on today? Time, TV schedule for March Madness game",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 6:50 p.m. ETTennessee basketball targets a fourth straight Sweet 16 appearance in the NCAA Tournament second round game against 3-seed Virginia on March 22 in Philadelphia.The Vols (23-11) halted Miami (OH)'s offense in a 78-56 first-round victory on March 20.UVA (30-5) finished with a 15-3 run to beat Wright State in the first round on March 20.The winner will play the Kentucky-Iowa State winner in the Sweet 16 on March 27 in Chicago.Here's how to watch the Tennessee basketball vs. Virginia March Madness game today, including time, TV schedule and streaming information: What channel is Tennessee basketball vs. Virginia March Madness on today?TV Channel: TNTLive stream: Sling, March Madness Live app, HBO MaxTennessee basketball vs. Virginia will broadcast nationally on TNT. Andrew Catalon and Steve Lappas will call the game in Philadelphia, with Evan Washburn reporting courtside. Streaming options for the game include Sling and HBO Max.Watch Tennessee vs. Virginia with Sling Tennessee basketball vs. Virginia March Madness game time todayDate: Sunday, March 22Start time: Approx. 6:10 p.m. Eastern/5:10 p.m. CentralThe Tennessee basketball vs. Virginia game starts at 6:10 p.m. Sunday from Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia. Tennessee basketball vs Virginia March Madness predictions, picks, oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Sunday, March 22Odds: Tennessee -1.5O/U: 137.5 pointsMoney line: Virginia -102, Tennessee -118 Tennessee Vols basketball schedule 2026Nov. 3: Mercer, W 76-61Nov. 8: Northern Kentucky, W 95-56Nov. 12: North Florida, W 99-66Nov. 17: Rice, W 91-66Nov. 20: Tennessee State, W 89-60Nov. 24: vs. Rutgers in Las Vegas, W 85-60Nov. 25: vs. Houston in Las Vegas, W 76-73Nov. 26: vs. Kansas in Las Vegas, L 81-76Dec. 2: at Syracuse, L 62-60Dec. 6: vs. Illinois in Nashville, L 75-62Dec. 16: Louisville, W 83-62Dec. 21: Gardner-Webb, W 94-52Dec. 30: SC State, W 105-54Jan. 3: at Arkansas, L 86-75Jan. 6: Texas, W 85-71Jan. 10: at 